---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="About Southwala" description="Southwala is a daily guide to panchangam, rasi phalalu, temples, the Bhagavad Gita and spiritual practice for Telugu, Kannada, Tamil and Malayalam homes.">
  <div class="page">
    <h1>About Southwala</h1>
    <p>Southwala is a daily guide for people who follow the Hindu calendar and want clear answers: what is today's tithi, when is Rahu Kalam, what does my rashi say, which temple should I visit, and what does the Gita teach about the problem in front of me. We write for homes in Andhra Pradesh, Telangana, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu and Kerala, and for families from the South living elsewhere.</p>
    <h2>What you will find here</h2>
    <p><b>Panchangam and timings</b> for your location, <b>rasi phalalu</b> for all twelve rashis every day, <b>Amavasya and Pournami</b> dates, <b>mantras with meanings</b>, <b>temple guides</b>, the <b>Bhagavad Gita</b> chapter by chapter, and daily articles on festivals, karma and yoga.</p>
    <h2>How the content is made</h2>
    <p>Timings are calculated from astronomical positions of the Sun and Moon using the Lahiri ayanamsa, then checked against published almanacs. Horoscopes follow the classical Vedic transit (gochara) rules. Articles draw on the Ramayana, Mahabharata, Bhagavad Gita and Puranas, and on common practice in the Telugu, Kannada, Tamil and Malayalam traditions. Practices differ between families and regions, so for rituals please confirm with your own priest or temple. Read our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>
    <h2>Talk to us</h2>
    <p>Corrections, suggestions and collaborations: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
